WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.603
-The president is peddling
another insane conspiracy theory

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.438
about the death toll
in Puerto Rico

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:08.875
as Republicans brace themselves
for the midterms.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.110
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look".

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.147 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.053
The president has been
going on TV basically every day

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.355
to try to convince people
that he's competent

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.323
as a potentially devastating
hurricane

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:25.725
bears down on the East Coast.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.661
Lately, he's taken to posting
videos to Twitter,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.729
but it's clear from
the quality of these videos

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:34.067
that he's just making his
staffers point a camera at him

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.535
while he rambles
off the top of his head.

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:38.438
Yesterday, for example,
he tried to reassure people

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:41.006
that his government was ready
for Hurricane Florence.

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:44.210
-Hurricane Florence
is fast approaching.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.780
It's going to be here
over the next 48 hours.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.417
We'll handle it.
We're ready. We're able.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.987
We've got the finest people,
I think, anywhere in the world.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.755
Get out of its way.

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:58.290
Don't play games with it.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.458
It's a big one.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:00.960
We are ready.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.128
But despite that,

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:04.630
bad things can happen

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:08.301
when you're talking about
a storm this size.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.036
It's called "Mother Nature".

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.971
You never know, but we know.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.707
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:18.778
-That video -- That video
is like a local news report

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.846
where the meteorologist
called in sick

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:23.515
and the sports guy had to
fill in at the last minute.

00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:26.553
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.757
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
The hurricane came to play,

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:36.629
but the first responders
left it all out on the field.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:40.900
In the end,
it comes down to turnovers.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.036
[ Normal ] If you want people
to take your message seriously,

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.804
maybe have higher
production quality

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.840
than a mid-level YouTube star.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.342
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
The storm is big.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.210
Get out of the way,
but before you do,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.979
please like and subscribe.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.980
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.751
[ Normal ]
And if that didn't do enough,

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.020
that didn't do enough to relieve
people's worst fears,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.590
the White House also released
this photo of Trump on the phone

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.560
while Chief of Staff John Kelly
and Vice President Mike Pence

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.229
look at some printouts.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.529
Oh, well, that's reassuring.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:13.232
They look like
they're ordering Chinese food.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.900
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
I'll go ahead and dial.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:21.507
You guys just pick four
or five things we can share.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.009
[ Normal ]
And as a life-threatening storm

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.343
bears down on the Easy Coast,

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:25.812
Trump has also been
bragging about

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:28.047
his handling of the humanitarian
disaster in Puerto Rico,

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:31.150
which left nearly 3,000
American citizens dead.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.220
Now, that is the official death
toll from an independent study

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.821
commissioned by Puerto Rico's
government,

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:38.725 line:0%
and yet, our deranged president
doesn't believe it.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.260 line:0%
-He says...

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.745 line:0%
He then says,
in a second tweet...

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.297
-That's the official death toll,
you lunatic.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:19.965
Now we know
why he's so orange --

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:22.968
his brain
is just melted pumpkin guts.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.303
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.806
-We don't need a book.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:30.810
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:33.312
-We don't need a book,
we don't need an anonymous op-ed

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:35.681
to tell us that the president
is an addled narcissist

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:38.784
who peddles one
conspiracy theory after another.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:40.753
He said the first black
president wasn't born here,

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.588
said three million people
voted illegally,

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:44.690
said Muslims celebrated on 9/11,

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:45.891
and thinks you get super powers

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.460
from staring
directly into the sun.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.128
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.030
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
May the power of the sky lamp

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:55.201
fill my muscles!

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.836
[ Normal ]
Now, Trump's incompetence

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.070
and erratic behavior

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.906
are posing major political
problems for Republicans

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.941
as the fall campaign season
gets underway.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.709
A slew of new polls

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:05.010
have given Democrats
a major edge

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.179
in the midterm elections.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.581
GOP Senate Majority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.583
even admitted this week that
some of those races

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.785
will be tough
for Republicans,

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.721
using a colorful metaphor.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:17.923 line:0%
-But we know this is gonna be
a very challenging election

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:21.026 line:0%
on the Senate side.

00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:23.662 line:0%
I'll just list you
a bunch of races

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.331
that are dead even.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:28.368
Arizona, Nevada, Tennessee,

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:31.437
Montana, North Dakota, Missouri,

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.306
Indiana, West Virginia,

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.240
and Florida.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.077
All of them too close to call,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.712
and every of them

00:04:40.712 --> 00:04:42.114
like a knife fight in an alley.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:44.283
I mean, just a brawl.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:46.452
-I seriously doubt
Mitch McConnell

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:49.254
has ever been in a fight...

00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:50.690
or in an alley.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.890
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.193
He should use a metaphor
he can relate to.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.194
[ Imitating Mitch McConnell ]
These elections are like when

00:04:56.194 --> 00:04:59.465
you order a steak medium-rare
and you get it medium

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:03.135
and your wife says you should
send it back,

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:04.803
but you just eat it,

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:07.339
and then your wife thinks
you're a coward.

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:08.807
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:10.242
But she doesn't say that.

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:14.880
She's just real quiet
the rest of the night.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:16.215
It's like that.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.082
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:19.418
[ Normal ] Now, one --

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.854
one of those knife fights

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.924
is happening in Texas,
where Democrat Beto O'Rourke

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.792
is running neck-and-no-neck

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:29.662
with Republican Senator
Ted Cruz.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.432
In public,
Republicans are bullish

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:34.934
on Cruz's reelection chances,

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.168
but this week,
we found out that

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:38.737
they are much more pessimistic
in private

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.005
after the "New York Times"

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:42.208
obtained private comments
from a top Trump aide

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.911
suggesting that Cruz might lose
because no one likes him.

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:47.346 line:0%
-At a private gathering
over the weekend,

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:49.047 line:0%
White House Budget Director
Mick Mulvaney

00:05:49.047 --> 00:05:51.016 line:0%
warned Republican donors
and party officials

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:53.518 line:0%
that they party was battling
serious vulnerabilities

00:05:53.518 --> 00:05:55.054 line:0%
in the upcoming midterms.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.489
According to
the "New York Times",

00:05:56.489 --> 00:06:00.493
Mulvaney raised the prospect
that Senator Ted Cruz of Texas

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.528
could actually
lose his bid for reelection

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:05.465
because he's not seen
as likable enough.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.834 line:0%
-He said this in private --

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.549
-So, Ted Cruz debased himself
by cozying up to Donald Trump --

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:28.354
a guy who insulted his wife
and said his dad killed JFK.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:32.358
And in return, they call him
unlikable behind his back.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.360
That is rough.
You know, I feel like I should

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.095
say something nice
about Ted Cruz

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.129
just to balance it out.

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:38.297
So, let me try.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.499
He's -- Let's see.

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:45.004
He's...

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.705
not here?

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:50.977
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:55.781
Now, Democrats face an uphill
battle to retake the Senate,

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:57.783
but if they're close in Texas,
they have a chance,

00:06:57.783 --> 00:06:59.918
which is why the GOP
is trying a new tactic

00:06:59.918 --> 00:07:01.254
to motivate their base --

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:03.422
dangling the threat
of impeachment.

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:05.458
Last week, for example,
Trump told his supporters that

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.160
if he's impeached
by a Democratic Congress,

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.695
it will be their fault.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.463 line:0%
-They like to use
the "impeach" word.

00:07:11.463 --> 00:07:13.065 line:0%
"Impeach Trump".
Maxine Waters --

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:15.467 line:0%
"We will impeach him,
but he didn't do anything wrong!

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:18.103 line:0%
It doesn't matter.
We will impeach him!"

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:20.105 line:0%
It's so ridiculous,

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:24.310 line:0%
but we'll worry about that
if it ever happens.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.944 line:0%
But if it does happen,
it's your fault

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:27.747 line:0%
'cause you didn't
go out to vote.

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:29.314
-I'm sorry,
real quick, real quick.

00:07:29.314 --> 00:07:31.250
Can we just go back
to that first part?

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.552 line:0%
-They like to use
the "impeach" word.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:36.455
-Yeah, that's the word.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:39.858
"Impeach" is the "impeach" word.

00:07:39.858 --> 00:07:41.427
Did you mean to say
"the I-word"?

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:43.762
Because that would make sense.

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:45.164
Trump has zero subtlety.

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:48.233
He's like a guy spelling out
dirty words around his kids.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:51.937
[ Imitating Donald Trump ]
She had nice b-o-o-b-s.

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:53.673
You know, boobs. Boobs.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:55.374
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.943
And Republicans
are also marshaling

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.710
every member of the Trump family
they can get,

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.145
like Donald Trump Jr.,

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:02.013
who's been campaigning for
Republicans across the country

00:08:02.013 --> 00:08:04.450
and did a rare sit-down
interview with ABC this week

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:05.551
about the midterms.

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.419 line:0%
-Trump Jr. says
the November midterms

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:09.955 line:0%
will inevitably
be a referendum on his father,

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:11.324 line:0%
one where historical odds

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.826 line:0%
suggest Democrats
could win back the House.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:16.461 line:0%
And he worries that could
spell political catastrophe

00:08:16.461 --> 00:08:17.763 line:0%
for his father.

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:19.664 line:0%
-So, our people,
the MAGA people,

00:08:19.664 --> 00:08:22.067 line:0%
they have to turn up.
They have to get out and vote.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.735 line:0%
And I think we can
break history.

00:08:23.735 --> 00:08:27.773
-Oh, I think
you broke it already.

00:08:27.773 --> 00:08:30.209
The rest of us are trying to
piece it back together

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:33.045
like a vase after a house party.

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:36.082
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.820
"What happened to your vase?"

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.356
"Oh, some douche came over
and drank beer out of it.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.158
And then I said
'You got to pay for my vase',

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:47.693
and he said, 'Do you know
who my dad is?'

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.394
And I said, 'Everyone knows
who your dad is

00:08:49.394 --> 00:08:51.063
because you have
the same name, dummy'.

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:53.165
And then he started to cry
and said 'I wish I was Ivanka',

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:54.500
so I felt bad and I said,
'It's okay,

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.734
you don't have to
pay for the vase',

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:57.402
and then he said, 'Sike!'
and broke another vase.

00:08:57.402 --> 00:09:00.672
He's a real [bleep]".

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:03.742
And Don Jr. isn't the only
Trump son showing up on TV

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:06.378
to support his father
and get Republicans out to vote.

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:08.480
Yesterday, Eric Trump
went on Fox News

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.382
and rambled about
the possibility that

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:13.653
Democrats might impeach Trump
if they win in November.

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:15.454
But the most jarring part
of that interview

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:18.323
came when Eric was asked about
famed journalist Bob Woodward's

00:09:18.323 --> 00:09:20.659
new book "Fear",
a damaging insider's account

00:09:20.659 --> 00:09:21.927
of the Trump White House,

00:09:21.927 --> 00:09:24.930
and he decided to toss out
some casual anti-Semitism

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.933
that was not only offensive,
but very hard to follow.

00:09:27.933 --> 00:09:31.036 line:0%
-You can write some
sensational nonsense book.

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:32.638 line:0%
CNN will definitely
have you on there

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:34.873 line:0%
because they love
to trash the president.

00:09:34.873 --> 00:09:36.675 line:0%
It'll mean you sell
three extra books,

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:38.243 line:0%
you make three extra shekels --

00:09:38.243 --> 00:09:40.245 line:0%
I mean, at the behest
of the American people,

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:43.248 line:0%
at the behest of our country.

00:09:43.248 --> 00:09:45.417
-Not only is that anti-Semitic,

00:09:45.417 --> 00:09:48.620
but you don't know what the word
"behest" means.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.122
[ Imitating Eric Trump ]
My father's amazing.

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:52.791
He's the "behest" president
we've ever had.

00:09:52.791 --> 00:09:54.927
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:54.927 --> 00:09:57.096
[ Normal ] But Democrats aren't
running on Woodward's book

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.264
or even impeachment, really.

00:09:58.264 --> 00:10:00.165
They're running entirely
on issues like healthcare

00:10:00.165 --> 00:10:02.301
and specifically,
Medicare for all --

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:04.437
an idea that not too long ago
was considered

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:06.204
a fringe pie-in-the-sky idea

00:10:06.204 --> 00:10:07.773
and is now so mainstream,

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:10.109
former president Obama
endorsed it last week.

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:13.112 line:0%
-Democrats aren't just
running on good old ideas

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:15.147 line:0%
like a higher minimum wage.

00:10:15.147 --> 00:10:17.115 line:0%
They're running on
good new ideas

00:10:17.115 --> 00:10:19.651 line:0%
like Medicare for all.
-Damn!

00:10:19.651 --> 00:10:21.120
When Bernie Sanders heard that,

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.089
he got so excited
his hair combed itself.

00:10:24.089 --> 00:10:27.126
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:29.594 --> 00:10:31.831
Who knows?

00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:33.498
Who knows what's gonna happen
in November?

00:10:33.498 --> 00:10:36.268
But this week has shown that
the choice could not be clearer.

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:37.836
I don't know if
the blue wave is coming,

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:39.605
but if it is,
the president better...

00:10:39.605 --> 00:10:41.406
-Get out of its way.

00:10:41.406 --> 00:10:43.275 line:0%
-This has been "A Closer Look".

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:46.278 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

